  "interpretation": {
    "v1_all32_LGB_only_-0.12_vs_T75": "Adding all 32 features (12 ReVol + 20 Savgol) to schemeP slightly hurts standalone LGB regression \u2014 likely because the 20 Savgol smoothers are redundant with existing EWMA/MA features in schemeP, adding noise to the 5-seed average.",
    "v2_revol12_LGB_only_+0.15_vs_T75": "ReVol-only (12 features, drop Savgol) gives a small +0.15 lift on standalone LGB. This is consistent with R44's prediction direction but at the LOW END of the +0.5~+2.5 expected range. Within typical seed-noise (T63/T67/T73/T76 noise floor was ~0.5).",
    "v4_revol_only6_LGB_only_+0.06_vs_T75": "Just the 6 wmp1-ReVol features (the T35 highest-gain group) gives essentially zero lift, showing that the marginal v2 gain comes from the COMBINATION of mid + wmp1 ReVol, not from the highest-gain features alone.",
    "ensemble_with_NN_no_gain": "When ensembled with T81 NN at the iter_014 weights, NONE of the three variants beats iter_014's +38.28. Best is v2 at +38.18 (-0.10) \u2014 within noise. The implication: the small standalone LGB lift is fully redundant with what the NN already captures.",
    "per_seed_variance": "Per-seed \u0394ev vs T75 is HIGH variance: v4 seed 42 = +5.09 but seed 7 = -1.97. The seed-mean is small (+0.30) and the high variance is itself a sign that ReVol is mostly fitting test-window noise rather than a stable signal.",
    "R44_F-F_pathway_status": "R44 said ReVol's CE F-F false-signal artifact would be REJECTED under regression. Confirmed: regression LGB rejects T35's catastrophic CE -0.77 hit (T91 v2 LGB = +0.15 vs T75). But the OTHER half of R44's hypothesis (ReVol becomes a TRUE signal under regression) is NOT supported \u2014 gain is within noise floor.",
    "next_steps_implication": "R44 top-3 (T35-revival) is essentially DEAD as an iter_015 candidate. Recommend reallocating budget to R44 top-1 (T46-CatBoost-regression \u2014 diversity from boosting algo difference is a stronger thesis) and top-2 (T22-alpha101 \u2014 alphas designed for regression-style targets at h=60)."
  }
